.max-w-prose
  = doc_info(url: "https://github.com/profoundry-us/rails-mini-profiler", icon: "chart-bar", icon_css: "text-error") do
    :markdown
      _Loco_**Motion** recommends **Rails Mini Profiler** — our maintained
      fork — to answer the only performance question that matters in
      development: *why* is this request slow?

.prose
  :markdown
    # Profiling

    Improving performance is three questions: what is slow, why is it slow,
    and did the fix work? Monitoring tools answer the first in production.
    [Rails Mini Profiler](https://github.com/profoundry-us/rails-mini-profiler)
    answers the second and third at your desk: a waterfall of every query,
    template, component render, and cache call in a request, plus a
    flamegraph, one click from the page you are looking at. This guide
    covers installing our fork, reading a profile, configuring it, and
    safely turning it on for a staging or production request when the
    slowness only happens there.

- # The roadmap: six sections plus the victory lap. The links opt out of
- # Turbo because the layout wraps pages in a turbo-frame, which would
- # otherwise swallow same-page anchor jumps.
.mt-8.rounded-box.border.border-base-300.p-6
